B.bc7=new A.P("YOUR TRIBUTARY",B.k)
B.bc8=new A.P("When turn 8 ends,"," the Danes' Great Heathen Army lands on East Anglia's coast \u2014 the kingdom they come to take (anywhere on England's east coast when you play East Anglia).")
B.bc9=new A.P("A scattered start"," (chosen when you pick your realm) gives every realm one random province with a Barracks and a small host; the rest is independent. Only the conquest goal counts, and no great Viking host lands.")
B.bca=new A.P("Tap an army"," to select it. Green provinces are ones it can march into \u2014 your own or an ally's. Red ones marked with crossed swords can be attacked.")
B.bcb=new A.P(null,"They refuse.")
B.bcd=new A.P("Gold"," comes from taxes \u2014 the more people, the more gold \u2014 and from markets, ports and mines. Manpower comes from your people, and more from barracks.")
B.bce=new A.P(0.3,B.nK)
B.bcf=new A.P("Rule 45 provinces."," Every realm wins this way.")
B.bcj=new A.P("","Your armies join only when one marches onto another, or when you press Combine.")
B.bck=new A.P("Submission:"," a realm you have beaten \u2014 down to its last province, with part of its homeland in your hands and an army of yours at its door \u2014 offers to submit. Accept, and its land, armies and treasury join your realm.")
B.bcl=new A.P("2 moves a turn:"," march twice, or march and then attack. Marching into highland takes both moves.")
B.bcn=new A.P(null,"No active game")
B.bcq=new A.P("","Now and then an event card asks you to choose.")
B.bcs=new A.P("","The handshake button at the top right opens the realms of Britain.")
